  "comments": "Two main groups are known, most probably minted by different mints.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1</span> - portrait and circular legend larger, thin script.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2</span> - portrait and circular legend smaller, thick script with bold serifs.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span> - all details larger, &quot;1&quot; in denomination tall.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span> - all details smaller and closer the center, &quot;1&quot; in denomination short with bold serifs.<br />\r\nPicture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637342fcdce92.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637342fcdce92.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"107\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Combinations</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1</span>: 2002, 2004, 2008.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>+<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2</span>: 2011, 2013.",
